# P09.22 — Foreign-fn ctor mangling + `#[rustc_cxx_wrapper]` opt-out.
#
# Builds on P09.3 (auto-export), P09.13 (`#[rustc_cxx_ctor]`),
# and P08b (Itanium mangler). Two compiler-side wins:
#
# 1. `#[rustc_cxx_ctor]` is now legal on foreign fns in
#    `extern "C++"` blocks. The Itanium mangler reads the class
#    name off the return type and emits `_ZN<class>C1E<args>`
#    — same output as the impl-method path. The
#    `cxx_class_native!` macro uses this to declare ctors
#    without a hand-rolled sret trampoline or `#[link_name]`.
#
# 2. `#[rustc_cxx_wrapper]` is a new attribute that opts an
#    inherent method on a `#[repr(cpp)]` type OUT of P09.3's
#    auto-export. Used by `cxx_class_native!` for thin wrapper
#    methods that forward to an `extern "C++"` decl of the same
#    method — the auto-export would otherwise collide with the
#    C++ side's definition (or self-recurse via Rust linking
#    back into itself).
#
# 3. Bonus: `compute_symbol_name` now checks `attrs.symbol_name`
#    BEFORE the Itanium auto-mangle path, so `#[link_name]` on
#    `extern "C++"` fns is actually respected. Prior ordering
#    silently swallowed the override.

